<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">lifestory</ansi>

Where you came from. Three questions at creation, each with a short tale:
your homeland, how you were brought up, and the trade you followed. They
are written once and stay that way.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">lifestory</ansi>             tells your story and what it gave you
  <ansi fg="command">lifestory choose</ansi>      writes it, if it is not written yet
                        (<ansi fg="command">cancel</ansi> stops with nothing written)
  <ansi fg="command">lifestory [player]</ansi>    who someone here is, at a glance

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What it gives</ansi>

A small start, never a lasting edge:

  Each answer gives +1 to a stat it names (your choice when it names
  two). No stat gains more than +2 from your story, so the three
  answers give at most +3 in all.
  Your trade (your background) gives a keepsake for your pack, and
  sometimes a first rung in a skill.

The tale is read back in your own pronouns. Other players see only the
three names, never the numbers.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What it opens</ansi>

Your trade is your background, and your homeland and upbringing count too.
They never make you stronger in a fight, but the road notices them:

  - A scene (<ansi fg="command">help events</ansi>) may offer a choice only someone with your
    background can make: a soldier talks to a deserter as one of his own,
    an acolyte knows the old words. A choice you cannot make shows as
    <ansi fg="black-bold">(closed: needs a leader who was a soldier)</ansi>; one you can shows your
    name and what opened it: <ansi fg="black-bold">(Mara, life story: a soldier)</ansi>.
  - Townsfolk who have heard of your deeds (<ansi fg="command">help townsfolk</ansi>) may
    mention it: a soldier who fells a beast hears about the drill.
  - Only you carry a life story. Companions do not, so a background
    choice is always yours to make, as the leader.

<ansi fg="command">lifestory</ansi> shows yours.

Characters made before life stories existed are asked once, when they next
log in. Skip it and <ansi fg="command">creation</ansi> or <ansi fg="command">lifestory choose</ansi> asks again whenever you like.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help appearance</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help stats</ansi>.
